.TH QCTRACK "1" "2026\-11\-19" "qctrack 0.1.0" "qctrack"
.SH NAME
qctrack \- audio quality scoring and fake\-bitrate detection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qctrack
[-h] [--version] {scan,rescore,profile} ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Audio quality scoring and fake\-bitrate detection.

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fBqctrack\fR \fI\,scan\/\fR
analyse files and folders
.TP
\fBqctrack\fR \fI\,rescore\/\fR
score a saved report.json again with another profile, without the audio
.TP
\fBqctrack\fR \fI\,profile\/\fR
scoring profiles

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'qctrack scan'\/\fR
usage: qctrack scan [\-h] [\-\-fail\-below SCORE] [\-\-color {auto,always,never}]
                    [\-\-csv [FILE]] [\-\-csv\-values] [\-\-csv\-bom] [\-\-html [FILE]]
                    [\-\-json [FILE]] [\-\-spectrograms] [\-o DIR] [\-\-silent]
                    [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-v] [\-\-quick] [\-j N]
                    [\-\-timeout SECONDS] [\-\-no\-cache] [\-\-follow\-links]
                    paths [paths ...]

.TP
\fBpaths\fR
files and folders (recursive)

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'qctrack scan'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-below\fR \fI\,SCORE\/\fR
exit with code 4 if any track scores below SCORE (0\-100)

.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI\,{auto,always,never}\/\fR
colour output; auto = on for a terminal unless NO_COLOR is set (default)

.TP
\fB\-\-csv\fR \fI\,[FILE]\/\fR
also write a CSV report (default report.csv); \-\-csv=\- writes it to standard
output and turns the screen output off

.TP
\fB\-\-csv\-values\fR
add a measured\-value column next to each factor score in the CSV

.TP
\fB\-\-csv\-bom\fR
start the CSV file with a UTF\-8 byte\-order mark

.TP
\fB\-\-html\fR \fI\,[FILE]\/\fR
also write a self\-contained HTML report (default report.html); \-\-html=\- writes
it to standard output and turns the screen output off

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fI\,[FILE]\/\fR
also write a JSON report with every measurement and score (default
report.json); \-\-json=\- writes it to standard output and turns the screen
output off

.TP
\fB\-\-spectrograms\fR
embed a spectrogram image per track in the HTML report (needs python3\-pillow;
makes the scan slower and the report larger)

.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR, \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
folder for report files with default names (default: current folder)

.TP
\fB\-\-silent\fR
no results or progress on the terminal

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI\,PROFILE\/\fR
scoring profile (default: user or bundled)

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
show measurements

.TP
\fB\-\-quick\fR
header\-only scan (pass 1)

.TP
\fB\-j\fR \fI\,N\/\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI\,N\/\fR
parallel workers (default: one per CPU core on SSDs, two on spinning disks and
network shares)

.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI\,SECONDS\/\fR
time budget per file (default 300); a slower file is an Error

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-cache\fR
ignore and do not update the result cache

.TP
\fB\-\-follow\-links\fR
follow symbolic links to folders

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'qctrack rescore'\/\fR
usage: qctrack rescore [\-h] [\-\-fail\-below SCORE] [\-\-color {auto,always,never}]
                       [\-\-csv [FILE]] [\-\-csv\-values] [\-\-csv\-bom]
                       [\-\-html [FILE]] [\-\-json [FILE]] [\-\-spectrograms]
                       [\-o DIR] [\-\-silent] [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-v]
                       [file]

.TP
\fBfile\fR
report.json to read (default: report.json in the output folder)

.SH OPTIONS \fI\,'qctrack rescore'\/\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-below\fR \fI\,SCORE\/\fR
exit with code 4 if any track scores below SCORE (0\-100)

.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI\,{auto,always,never}\/\fR
colour output; auto = on for a terminal unless NO_COLOR is set (default)

.TP
\fB\-\-csv\fR \fI\,[FILE]\/\fR
also write a CSV report (default report.csv); \-\-csv=\- writes it to standard
output and turns the screen output off

.TP
\fB\-\-csv\-values\fR
add a measured\-value column next to each factor score in the CSV

.TP
\fB\-\-csv\-bom\fR
start the CSV file with a UTF\-8 byte\-order mark

.TP
\fB\-\-html\fR \fI\,[FILE]\/\fR
also write a self\-contained HTML report (default report.html); \-\-html=\- writes
it to standard output and turns the screen output off

.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fI\,[FILE]\/\fR
also write a JSON report with every measurement and score (default
report.json); \-\-json=\- writes it to standard output and turns the screen
output off

.TP
\fB\-\-spectrograms\fR
embed a spectrogram image per track in the HTML report (needs python3\-pillow;
makes the scan slower and the report larger)

.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR, \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
folder for report files with default names (default: current folder)

.TP
\fB\-\-silent\fR
no results or progress on the terminal

.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI\,PROFILE\/\fR
scoring profile (default: user or bundled)

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
show measurements

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'qctrack profile'\/\fR
usage: qctrack profile [\-h] {show\-default,validate} ...

.SH
POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS \fI\,'qctrack profile'\/\fR
.TP
\fBqctrack profile\fR \fI\,show\-default\/\fR
print the default profile
.TP
\fBqctrack profile\fR \fI\,validate\/\fR
check a profile file

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'qctrack profile show\-default'\/\fR
usage: qctrack profile show\-default [\-h]

.SH COMMAND \fI\,'qctrack profile validate'\/\fR
usage: qctrack profile validate [\-h] file

.TP
\fBfile\fR
profile to check

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All files were analysed.
.TP
.B 1
Some files were Error or Unsupported.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error or invalid profile.
.TP
.B 3
Fatal error, such as an unwritable output file.
.TP
.B 4
\fB\-\-fail\-below\fR was given and a track scored below the limit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, colour output is off when \fB\-\-color\fR is \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base folder of the user profile (default \fI~/.config\fR).
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base folder of the result cache (default \fI~/.local/share\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/qctrack/profile.toml
User scoring profile, used when \fB\-\-profile\fR is not given. Without it the bundled default profile applies.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/qctrack/cache.db
Result cache. \fB\-\-no\-cache\fR ignores it.
.SH EXAMPLES
Scan a folder and write a CSV and an HTML report:
.PP
.RS
.nf
qctrack scan ~/Music \-\-csv \-\-html
.fi
.RE
.PP
Script a check that fails when any track scores below 70:
.PP
.RS
.nf
qctrack scan \-\-silent \-\-fail\-below 70 album/
.fi
.RE
.PP
Rescore saved measurements with another profile, without the audio:
.PP
.RS
.nf
qctrack scan ~/Music \-\-json
qctrack rescore \-\-profile strict.toml
.fi
.RE
